.TH DNS_DTD 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
dns_domain_todot_cat, dns_domain_todot_inline, dns_domain_todot \- Convert DNS domain names to dot-separated format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/dns.h>

.IB int
.IB dns_domain_todot_cat(stralloc* out, const char* d);

.IB unsigned int
.IB dns_domain_todot_inline(char* x);

.IB unsigned int
.IB dns_domain_todot(char* out, const char* in);

.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions provide a set of operations for converting DNS domain names to dot-separated format.

.TP
.IB dns_domain_todot_cat
Appends a DNS domain name in wire format to an output string, converting it to dot-separated format.

.TP
.IB dns_domain_todot_inline
In-place converts a DNS domain name in wire format to dot-separated format.

.TP
.IB dns_domain_todot
Converts a DNS domain name in wire format to dot-separated format and stores the result in an output buffer.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBdns_domain_todot_cat\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/dns.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>

int main() {
    stralloc sa;
    stralloc_init(&sa);
    const char* in = "example.com";

    if (dns_domain_todot_cat(&sa, in) != 1) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error: dns_domain_todot_cat failed\n");
        return 1;
    }

    printf("Converted domain name: %s\n", sa.s);

    stralloc_free(&sa);

    return 0;
}
.nef